Bug: `set(s1)` strips duplicate character counts; `set('aab')` and `set('abb')` both evaluate to `{'a', 'b'}`, incorrectly returning True. Corrected implementation:
```python
from collections import Counter
def is_anagram(s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:
    if len(s1) != len(s2):
        return False
    return Counter(s1) == Counter(s2)
```
This runs in O(n) time and O(k) space, strictly validating character counts.

